::Q001::[markdown]τόν:{
	~%100%masc. acc. sing. of the definite article “the”#Correct: **τόν** is masc. acc. sing. of the definite article “the” (Chapter 1).
	~%-100%fem. acc. pl. of the definite article “the”#Incorrect. The fem. acc. pl. of the definite article “the” is **τάς** (Ch. 1).
	~%-100%neut. gen. pl. of the definite article “the”#Incorrect. The neut. gen. pl. of the definite article “the” is **τῶν** (Ch. 1).
	~%-100%masc. nom. sing. of the definite article “the”#Incorrect. The masc. nom. sing. of the definite article “the” is **ὁ** (Ch. 1).
	~%-100%masc. gen. sing. of the definite article “the”#Incorrect. The masc. gen. sing. of the definite article “the” is **τοῦ** (Ch. 1).
}


::Q002::[markdown]masc. acc. sing. of the adjective “good; noble”:{
	~%-100%ἄξια#Incorrect. **ἄξια** is the neut. acc. pl. of the adjective “worthy” (Ch. 4).
	~%-100%ἄξιον#Incorrect. **ἄξιον** is the masc. acc. sing. of the adjective “worthy” (Ch. 4).
	~%-100%ἀγαθαί#Incorrect. **ἀγαθαί** is the fem. nom. pl. of the adjective “good; noble” (Ch. 4).
	~%100%ἀγαθόν#Correct: **ἀγαθόν** is the correct form for masc. acc. sing. of the adjective “good; noble” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%ἀξίου#Incorrect. **ἀξίου** is the masc. gen. sing. of the adjective “worthy” (Ch. 4).
}


